{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"fulltime-determined-wren","creation_channel":"cli","description":"ADP is a general-purpose platform. A target repository it is piloted against must not appear in its committed configuration.\n\n`compose.override.yaml` is tracked and names a client repository four times. Line 78 mounts `../archive-massgov-pfml:/repos/archive-massgov-pfml` into `activity-worker`, line 113 mounts it read-only into the repository-intelligence services, and lines 91 and 116 register it in `REPO_INTELLIGENCE_REPOS`. Line 76 carries a comment naming the client product. These sit beside the platform's own `agentic-demo-*` mounts, which belong there.\n\n`config/local/checks.yaml` is tracked while every other operator-edited config in that directory is not. `.gitignore` lines 8-26 establish the convention that the platform ships a `.yaml.example` template and ignores the operator's `.yaml`, applied to `github`, `jira`, `integrations`, `gates`, `gate_engine`, `tickets`, and `review-trust-root`. `checks.yaml` ships a `checks.yaml.example` but has no ignore pair, so it was committed. The operator's copy carries a client entry and is held back only by a `skip-worktree` bit, which also hides local edits from `git status`.\n\nProject compose overlays have no ignore rule. The pilot overlay is excluded through `.git/info/exclude`, which lives outside the repository and protects one checkout. A fresh clone has no such protection.\n\n`README.md:132` and `tests/unit/test_intake_base.py:64` carry `base:joeoakhart/PFMLPB-33758`, which is a personal account name and a client ticket key.\n\nClient repository names also appear as sample values in nine test fixtures. Those encode no client behaviour and are out of scope here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No tracked file under version control names the client repository, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_repo_hygiene.py -k no_tracked_file_names_a_client_repository`\n- [ ] No tracked file under version control carries a personal home directory path or account name, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_repo_hygiene.py -k no_tracked_file_carries_a_personal_account_path`\n- [ ] Every operator-edited config in the config directory has an ignore rule paired with a shipped example, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_repo_hygiene.py -k every_operator_config_is_ignored_and_has_an_example`\n- [ ] Project compose overlays are ignored while the platform's own compose files stay tracked, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_repo_hygiene.py -k project_compose_overlays_are_ignored`\n- [ ] The documented base branch example uses a neutral account and ticket, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_intake_base.py -k declared_base_preserves_the_supplied_branch`\n\n## Testing\nRun each acceptance criterion selector on its own. Run `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/inv ci` before closing the ticket.","id":"d55f-8e10-fdcb-4f97","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["adp","hygiene","config"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Remove client-specific configuration and personal paths from tracked platform files"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1790012314269024001,"uuid":"f1a46618-bba3-494f-bb9d-fdb76fcff795"}